@@appendix

# Conventions and normalisations {#app:conv}

This appendix reconciles the notations of the different agents and fixes every factor. The main text uses one convention throughout (the canonical one below); each source file is mapped to it.

## The kernel normalisations {#app:norm}

@table tab:norms | Kernel normalisations in the different sources and their relations. $c$ is the frame scalar (\ref{eq:cfactor}); $M=P^3p_{0,\lambda_2+1}$.
@size small
@cols p{2.3cm}p{4.6cm}p{7cm}
| symbol | where | definition and relation |
|---|---|---|
| $K$ | G1, P4, main text | $c\,Q_{\rm num}M_1M_2=\sum K\,m\,m$, $m_{kl}=P^3p_{kl}$, $M$ exactly (no extra factor) |
| $G$ | D1, D2, D3 | $4c\,Q_{\rm num}M_1M_2=\sum G\,N\,N$ (D2's "$4c$"); for the adjoint $G=4K$, because $M_{\rm vac}=2h^2P^3p_{02}$ per site in the XXX limit and $2\times2=4$ |
| $G^s$ | U2 | $G^s:=G/4=K$ ($c\,Q_{\rm num}M_1M_2=\sum G^sNN$; U2 states "G of the spec = D2's printed G divided by 4") |
| $\Theta$ | G1, D3 | $\Theta=K/(\omega_1\omega_1')^{2\lambda_1-\lambda_2}$, a polynomial in $(a,a',t)=(1/\omega_1,1/\omega_1',1/\theta_{12})$; adjoint: $\Theta=G/(4\omega_1^3\omega_1'^3)$ (D3, exact in 25/25 entries) |
| $Q_{\rm num}$ | all | $\langle\Phi_\infty|\Psi\rangle/\langle x_0^G|\Psi\rangle$ in the diagonal frame; companion-frame version $Q_{\rm num}^{\rm comp}=Q_{\rm num}/(\kappa^G\kappa^{G\prime})=c\,Q_{\rm num}/(\omega_1\omega_1')^{2\lambda_1-\lambda_2}$ (D1, D3) |
| $T(B)$ | D1 | $\langle\Phi_\infty|\Psi\rangle D_B(\omega_0)/\langle\Omega_0\otimes\Omega_0|\Psi\rangle=c_T(\zeta)\,Q_{\rm num}M_1M_2$ |
| $\nu$ | U2 | $N_i/M=(1,\kappa,\pi,\kappa\pi,\varepsilon_s)$; the main text writes $\nu$ for this vector, and $\nu(u)=\Pi(u)$ appears only in the XXX $B$-operator discussion (Section~\ref{sec:Bxxx}) |
| $D_2$ | W2, W3 | the quadratic localising algebra; not to be confused with D2 (agent) or $D_B$ ($\det N$) |
| $\gamma_2,\gamma_3,d_3$ | this text | Frobenius coefficients of $f_0,f_2$ (U2 calls $\gamma_2,\gamma_3$ "$c_2,c_3$"; renamed to avoid the clash with the double pole $c_2$) |
@endtable

The relation $\Theta^{\rm adj}=G/(4\omega^3\omega'^3)$ was found by D3 to be exact; G1 verified symbolically in 25/25 entries that $\Theta$ defined from $K$ equals it, so no further factor hides in the conventions. The "4 of D2/D3" is a convention, not physics: with $M=P^3p_{0,\lambda_2+1}$ exactly one uses $K=G/4$ and no 4 appears anywhere.

## Frames and bases {#app:basis}

- *Frames.* Diagonal frame: states of the diagonal-twist Hamiltonians; companion frame: $\Psi_c=(P_{\rm phys}^{-1}\otimes P_{\rm phys}^{-1})|_{z=\zeta}\Psi_d$, $x_0^c=e_1\otimes e_1$ (D3), $\Phi^\infty_c=\Omega_c^\infty[\omega_1]\otimes\Omega_c^\infty[\omega_1']$. $x_0^G$ in the diagonal frame is $x(\zeta)\otimes x(\zeta)$ and $\langle x_0^c|\Psi_c\rangle=\langle x_0^d|\psi_d\rangle$.
- *Basis orders.* Notebook (W-agents, data files): GT patterns descending, index 1 or 0 is the HW ket; `gl3_reps` (P, D, G, U agents): lowest weight first, HW ket last. Adjoint map $\mathrm{NB}\to\mathtt{gl3}$: $(7,5,6,4,2,1,3,0)$ (0-based). Weights in notebook order for the adjoint: $(2,1,0),(2,0,1),(1,2,0),(1,1,1),(1,1,1),(1,0,2),(0,2,1),(0,1,2)$; the metric diagonal $G=(1,1,1,2,6,9,4,9)$. U2's slices (`gl3` index $\nu$): top $C_7$, $(4,1,1)\ C_5$, $(3,3,0)\ C_6$, octets $(C_2,C_4)$, singlet $C_0$; W4's (notebook, 1-based): $C_1,C_2,C_3,(C_5,C_4)$ resp. $(C_4,C_5)$, $C_8$; Table~\ref{tab:cg} uses W4's.
- *Signs.* HW kets are G-normalised with the first non-zero component, in descending GT order, positive (D1, U2); W4's canonical HW kets are primitive integer vectors (first non-zero component positive). For $(4,4,2)$ of $[3,2,0]$ the exact slice has an exactly vanishing component and the chain branch's sign convention differs; the CG cells align signs and use norm-based errors (W3).
- *Copies.* In a multiplicity-2 sector copy 1 is the eigenvector of $S3c[1,2]$ with the smaller eigenvalue ($\alpha_1^{(0)}$); U1's "copy 0" is W4's copy 1 and $\sqrt5\to-\sqrt5$ exchanges the copies.
- *$\theta_{12}$ units.* U1's series are in units $\theta_{12}=1$, with $H^{(n)},a^{(n)}\sim\theta_{12}^{n-1}$, $b^{(n)}\sim\theta_{12}^{n-2}$; W4's data are $\theta$-scaled, $H=\eta/\theta_{12}$, $a=\alpha/\theta_{12}$, $b=\beta/\theta_{12}^2$, with $\theta=(2/7,-3/5)$, $\theta_{12}=31/35$ for the numerical tables and series (so "$140/31$" is $4/\theta_{12}$).
- *Kernel pair orders.* G1: lexicographic pairs $(kl)$, $0\le k<l\le\lambda_1+1$, $l\ge\lambda_2+1$. D2/D1: $N=(P^3p_{02},P^{3\prime}p_{02},P^3p_{03},P^{3\prime}p_{03},P^3p_{23})$; the map to G1's order $(02),(03),(12),(13),(23)$ is $1\to(02)$, $2\to(12)$, $3\to(03)$, $4\to(13)$, $5\to(23)$ because $P^{3\prime}p_{0l}=P^3p_{1l}$.
- *$c$ for general $\Lambda$:* (\ref{eq:cfactor}); wrong exponents tested and excluded (Section~\ref{sec:frames}).

## Numerical points and grids {#app:grids}

- $\theta=(2/7,-3/5)$, $\theta_{12}=31/35$; $\theta$ variants for kernel laws: $(1/5,-4/9)$, $(3/7,-1/4)$, $(1/2,-1/3)$, $(-1/7,-6/5)$, $(4/5,-2/3)$ ($\theta_{12}=29/45,19/28,5/6,37/35,22/15$); further $\theta_{12}$ values $7/9,13/8,-9/7,-17/10,11/6,3/4,-5/3,19/13,-7/11,9/5,-13/9,25/14,-19/10,15/11,-11/7$ (G1, 12--20 values); pairs with equal $\theta_{12}$: $(2/7,-3/5),(-1/3,-128/105),(5/4,51/140)$.
- Twist points: $P=(3/2,5/4,2/3)$, $P'=(2,5/3,-1/2)$, $X_1=(7/5,-3/4,1/6)$, $X_2=(-4/3,2/9,5/7)$, $X_3=(1/3,-2/7,5/11)$; further $X_4..X_6$ and 26 real-spectrum random rationals (D1); some triples give a complex spectrum of $S_2+\pi S_3$ and are skipped.
- Vacuum twists: $\omega=(5/2,7/3,3/5)$, $\omega'=(7/4,-2/5,9/7)$; $\omega_0=(5/2,7/3,3/5)$ for $T(B)$; $(\omega_1,\omega_1')$: base $(5/2,7/4)$, second $(-2/5,3)$, a $3\times3$ grid $\omega_1\in\{5/2,-2/5,9/7\}\times\omega_1'\in\{7/4,3,-5/3\}$, a 9-value grid $\{5/2,-2/5,9/7,3,-5/3,7/4,11/3,-7/2,13/5\}$ (72 ordered pairs), and G1's $w'$ list up to $23/9,-3/2,10/3$.
- Regime: $\phi=(1/3,-2/7,5/11)$, control $\phi'=(-2/5,3/8,7/11)$; $\hat\omega_1\in\{3/4,-5/3,1/2,-7/3\}$, $\hat\omega_1'\in\{-12/5,7/2,1/8,5/4\}$ (the 24-point Stage-D grid is $\{3/4,-5/3\}\times\{-1/5,9/7,5/3\}$ for $\hat\omega$ and $\{-12/5,7/2\}\times\{1/8,-3/4\}$ for $\hat\omega'$); $\epsilon\in\{1,2,4\}\cdot10^{-6}$ (chain-side, three values) and $\epsilon_k=10^{-6}2^{-k}$, $k=0..11$ (series fits, $K=12$; the extended set $K=24$, 400 digits, reliable to $n=18$).
- Generic points for operator identities: $u_0=3/7$, $u_1=-2/9$ (note: Laurent fits at $\theta_1=3/7=u_0$ hit a pole).
- Precision: chain 200 digits; Q side 60 (finite twist), 80 (fits, kernels), 100--120 (regime), 200 (series), 400 (extended series); fixed-point 320-bit integer QR in D1; exact Fractions in D3, G1 (one-site).

