# The kernels {#app:K}

## The adjoint kernel {#app:Kadj}

@include gen/tab-G210.src

@include gen/tab-Gtw.src

For the adjoint the canonical $\Theta$ is $G/(4\omega_1^3\omega_1'^3)$ with $\omega=1/a$. A few entries in this normalisation (G1's K0 table, pairs $(02),(03),(12),(13),(23)$, $a'=a$ primed, $t=1/\theta_{12}$): $\Theta_{(02)(02)}=1+(a-a')t-3aa't^2$, $\Theta_{(02)(03)}=-a'(2at+1)/2$, $\Theta_{(03)(02)}=a(2a't-1)/2$, $\Theta_{(03)(03)}=aa'/4$, $\Theta_{(23)(23)}=a^3a'^3/4$, $\Theta_{(13)(13)}=-a^2a'^2(3aa't^2-at+a't-1)$, $\Theta_{(03)(23)}=aa'^3(6a^2t^2+4at+1)/4$. The full table follows from $G$ above or from the exchange rule $\Theta_{ij}(a,a',t)=\Theta_{ji}(a',a,-t)$; all 25 entries are stored exactly in `general_kernel_rep_210.pkl`.

## $[3,1,0]$ and $[3,2,0]$: base-point kernels {#app:K310}

The exact kernel $K$ at the base point $(\omega_1,\omega_1',\theta_{12})=(5/2,7/4,31/35)$ was evaluated from G1's stored exact polynomial laws (`general_kernel_rep_310.pkl`) in the basis of pairs $(02),(03),(04),(12),(13),(14),(23),(24),(34)$, rows $i$ and columns $j$; $K_{99}=1/9$. By the block theorem (\ref{eq:blockK}) the kernel of $[3,2,0]$ is the sub-block with rows and columns $(03),(04),(13),(14),(23),(24),(34)$ (we verified exact equality of all 49 entries, at this point and at $(-2/5,3,29/45)$); it reproduces the base-point values printed by P4 (for example $K_{11}=-2477531875/3936256$, $K_{12}=-15649375/95232$, $K_{17}=1241317375/2770563$, $K_{71}=-3124391459/709264128$, $K_{77}=1/9$ in the $[3,2,0]$ order).

@include gen/K310.src

Laws (all verified, Table~\ref{tab:laws} and Section~\ref{sec:structure}): each entry is a polynomial in $(\omega_1,\omega_1')$. For $[3,2,0]$ the table of total degrees is rows $8,7,7,6,6,5,4$ / $7,6,6,5,5,4,3$ (twice) / $6,5,5,4,4,3,2$ (twice) / $5,4,4,3,3,2,1$ / $4,3,3,2,2,1,0$, i.e.\ $d_{ij}=8-(e_i+e_j)$ with $e=(0,1,1,2,2,3,4)$, at most degree 4 in each of $\omega_1,\omega_1'$; for $[3,1,0]$, $e=(0,1,2,1,2,3,3,4,5)$, bidegree $(5,10)$ in $(1/\omega_1',t)$ at fixed $a$, 998 monomials; the dependence on $\theta$ is through $\theta_{12}$ only (equal-$\theta_{12}$ pairs agree to $4.8\cdot10^{-72}$, $8\cdot10^{-70}$, $2.4\cdot10^{-68}$ for $[2,1,0],[2,0,0],[3,2,0]$).

# The one-site kernel {#app:C}

Table~\ref{tab:onesite} lists the coefficients of $\theta_{kl}(a)=c_{kl}a^{k+l-\lambda_2-1}$ for all two-row and one-row representations up to $\lambda_1=4$. They are computed from the closed form (\ref{eq:ckl}); we cross-checked the entries printed by G1 for $[1,0,0],[1,1,0],[2,0,0],[2,1,0],[2,2,0],[3,1,0],[3,2,0],[4,2,0]$ (they agree).

