Other pitfalls recorded by the agents: a numerically vanishing feature ($p_{01}\sim10^{-78}$) must be zeroed explicitly before QR or it is counted as an independent feature; the $100$-digit regime solver needs a kernel threshold of $10^{-50}$ (the default $10^{-35}$ gives spurious lower degrees); a threshold-based degree reading of $q$ fails when the leading coefficient is $\epsilon$-suppressed (read the smallest degree admitting a kernel); the memoised `laurent` cache holds bad values after a fit at a pole; the mp eigensolver returns $10^{-59}$ imaginary noise in some sectors; the all-stage Python run stalled under contention. The notebooks were built from JSON and run cell by cell in the shared kernel (wolfbook new-notebook workaround), hence no native outputs.

The sources of this document are the plans `Gaudin-sl3-CG-plan.md`, `-round2-`, `-round3-`, `-round4-`, `-round5-plan.md`, the ten `RESULTS-*.md` files, the four notebooks and the six data files named above, and the repository's `HANDOFF.md` (entries from "sl(3) GAUDIN" onwards). The generator of this document (hand-written prose plus tables built from the data files) lives in `Paul/Mathematica/Gaudin/notes-src/`.
